Article 5 The work responsibilities of the people's governments at all levels in the prevention of juvenile delinquency are:
(1) formulating work plans for the prevention of juvenile delinquency;
(2) organizing relevant departments such as public security, education, civil affairs, culture and tourism, market regulation, cyberspace administration, health, press and publication, film, radio and television, and judicial administration to carry out the work of preventing juvenile delinquency;
(3) providing policy support and financial guarantees for the work of preventing juvenile delinquency;
(4) inspecting the implementation of this Law and the execution of work plans;
(5) organizing and carrying out publicity and education on the prevention of juvenile delinquency;
(6) other work responsibilities for the prevention of juvenile delinquency.

Article 28 For the purposes of this Law, "不良 conduct" means the following acts committed by a minor that are detrimental to his or her healthy growth:
(1) smoking or drinking alcohol;
(2) repeatedly skipping classes or playing truant;
(3) staying out all night without justifiable reason or running away from home;
(4) being addicted to the Internet;
(5) associating with persons with不良 habits in society, or organizing or participating in gangs that commit不良 conduct;
(6) entering places where minors are not allowed to enter according to laws and regulations;
(7) participating in gambling or disguised gambling, or engaging in feudal superstitious or cult activities;
(8) reading, watching, or listening to books, audio-visual products, or online information that propagate obscenity, pornography, violence, terror, extremism, or the like;
(9) other不良 conduct that is detrimental to the healthy physical and mental growth of minors.

Article 31 With respect to minor students who have committed不良 conduct, schools shall strengthen management and education and shall not discriminate against them; where a student refuses to correct or the circumstances are serious, the school may, depending on the circumstances, impose a disciplinary sanction or take the following management and education measures:
(1) giving admonition;
(2) requiring compliance with specific codes of conduct;
(3) requiring participation in specific thematic education;
(4) requiring participation in on-campus service activities;
(5) requiring acceptance of psychological counseling and behavioral intervention by social workers or other professionals;
(6) other appropriate management and education measures.

Article 38 For the purposes of this Law, "serious不良 conduct" means acts committed by a minor that are provided for in the Criminal Law but for which criminal punishment is not imposed due to the minor not having reached the statutory age of criminal responsibility, and the following acts that seriously endanger society:
(1) engaging in gang fights, chasing or intercepting others, forcibly taking or demanding property, or willfully damaging or occupying public or private property, or other acts of picking quarrels and provoking trouble;
(2) illegally carrying firearms, ammunition, crossbows, daggers, or other controlled instruments as prescribed by the State;
(3) beating, insulting, intimidating, or intentionally injuring the body of another person;
(4) stealing, looting, snatching, or intentionally damaging public or private property;
(5) disseminating obscene books, audio-visual products, or information;
(6) engaging in prostitution or patronizing prostitution, or performing obscene acts;
(7) using or injecting drugs, or providing drugs to others;
(8) participating in gambling with relatively large stakes;
(9) other acts that seriously endanger society.

Article 41 With respect to a minor who has committed serious不良 conduct, the public security organ may, depending on the specific circumstances, take the following correctional education measures:
(1) giving a reprimand;
(2) ordering an apology and compensation for losses;
(3) ordering a written statement of repentance;
(4) ordering regular reports on activities;
(5) ordering compliance with specific codes of conduct and prohibiting the commission of specific acts, contact with specific persons, or entry into specific places;
(6) ordering acceptance of psychological counseling and behavioral correction;
(7) ordering participation in social service activities;
(8) ordering acceptance of social observation, with social organizations and relevant institutions educating, supervising, and controlling the minor in appropriate places;
(9) other appropriate correctional education measures.

Article 44 Where a minor falls under any of the following circumstances, upon evaluation and approval by the specialized education steering committee, the education administrative department together with the public security organ may decide to send the minor to a specialized school for specialized education:
(1) committing acts that seriously endanger society, with flagrant circumstances or causing serious consequences;
(2) repeatedly committing acts that seriously endanger society;
(3) refusing to accept or cooperate with the correctional education measures prescribed in Article 41 of this Law;
(4) other circumstances provided for by laws or administrative regulations.
